{
  "id": "V15",
  "title": "Deflection and story drift",
  "intent": "Two unequal walls at one story with Cd, Ie and risk category entered. Checks every SDPWS Eq. 4.3-1 term (bending, shear, holdown slip, crushing) at 1.0E, that the story drift uses the largest wall δ, and δx = Cd·δxe/Ie against Δa = 0.020·h_sx (ASCE 7-22 Table 12.12-1, RC II). Passing case — no drift sizing.",
  "covers": [
    "SDPWS 2021 Eq. 4.3-1",
    "ASCE 7-22 §12.8.6",
    "ASCE 7-22 Table 12.12-1",
    "HDUE slip δ·T/cap",
    "Plate crushing (r < 0.73)"
  ],
  "handCalc": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "text": "Capacity distribution: both walls start at the same nailing, so V splits by length: V_1 = 6 × 10/18 = 3.333 k, V_2 = 6 × 8/18 = 2.667 k."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "text": "ASD unit shear v = 0.7·V/L = 233.33 plf on both walls (equal by construction) ≤ 312 plf → 6\" o.c., D/C = 0.748. h/b = 1.0 and 1.25 ≤ 2 → C_hb = 1."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "text": "Hardware: T = 0.7·V·h/L − 0.46·R_D. SW-1: 0.7 × 3.333 − 0.46 × 0.50 = 2.103 k → HDUE3; SW-2: 0.7 × 3.333 − 0.46 × 0.40 = 2.149 k → HDUE3. Posts: C ≤ 5.00 k → (2)2x4 (HDUE3 minimum post), A = 10.5 in²."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "text": "SW-1: v = 333.33 plf, T = C = 3333.33 lb, A = 10.5 in², G_a = 16 k/in → 8vh³/(EAb) = 8 × 333.33 × 10³ / (1,700,000 × 10.5 × 10) = 0.0149; vh/(1000G_a) = 333.33 × 10 / (1000 × 16) = 0.2083; Δ_HD = 0.127 × 3333.33 / 3790 = 0.1117; r = 3333.33 / (10.5 × 625) = 0.5079 < 0.73 → Δ_c = 0.02 × r / 0.73 = 0.0139; h·Δa/b = 10 × (0.1117 + 0.0139) / 10 = 0.1256 → δ = 0.3489 in."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "text": "SW-2: v = 333.33 plf, T = C = 3333.33 lb, A = 10.5 in², G_a = 16 k/in → 8vh³/(EAb) = 8 × 333.33 × 10³ / (1,700,000 × 10.5 × 8) = 0.0187; vh/(1000G_a) = 333.33 × 10 / (1000 × 16) = 0.2083; Δ_HD = 0.127 × 3333.33 / 3790 = 0.1117; r = 3333.33 / (10.5 × 625) = 0.5079 < 0.73 → Δ_c = 0.02 × r / 0.73 = 0.0139; h·Δa/b = 10 × (0.1117 + 0.0139) / 8 = 0.1570 → δ = 0.3840 in."
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "text": "Story drift: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-2 0.3840 in (the shorter wall deflects more at the same unit shear: 8vh³/EAb and h·Δa/b grow with 1/b)."
    },
    {
      "step": 7,
      "text": "δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.3840 / 1 = 1.5361 in. Δa = 0.020 × h_sx = 0.020 × 10 × 12 = 2.400 in (Table 12.12-1, RC II). δx/h_sx = 0.0128 → 1.5361 ≤ 2.400 OK, no drift upsizing."
    },
    {
      "step": 8,
      "text": "Line checks G1–G12 pass (5 → 6 k all to the foundation, self-weight only)."
    }
  ],
